course: dictionary
lesson: 9125
title: Smother: one word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Smother has more than one meaning, so the context tells you which one you need. Its basic idea is covering something so that air cannot reach it. «Fire needs oxygen too: a flame goes out when its air is cut off, which is how a fire blanket smothers a fire.» Here smother means to put out a fire by covering it.
explain: «Chips smothered in sauce» does not mean the chips are stopped from breathing. Check the clues: the sauce is spread thickly over the top, and nobody is hurt. Smothered here means covered thickly.
explain: Smother can also describe love. To smother someone with love is to give them so much attention that they feel trapped. Ask yourself: is anything being covered, or is someone feeling trapped? That question will guide you to the right meaning.
fact: Smother means to cover something so that air cannot reach it.
fact: «Smother the flames» means putting out a fire by cutting off its air.
fact: «Smothered in» means covered thickly, as in «chips smothered in sauce».
fact: A fire blanket smothers a small fire; never pour water on burning oil.
fact: Babies must not sleep under heavy blankets or with pillows, because they could be smothered.
exercise: «A fire blanket smothers a small fire by cutting off oxygen.» What does smothers mean here? | Lights it again | Makes it louder | Makes it burn brighter | *Puts out by covering it so no air reaches it
exercise: «The chips were smothered in gravy.» What does smothered mean? | Stopped from breathing | Put out | Cooked slowly | *Covered thickly
exercise: Find and copy the word from «Damaged cables smothered under bedding are warning signs» that means covered up. | *smothered | warning | cables | signs
test: Why does a fire go out when it is smothered? | *Because its air is cut off | Because it is too hot | Because it gets too much water
test: Someone says, «Mum smothers me with love.» What does it suggest? | She is hurt | *She gives so much attention that it feels trapped | Mum is cooking | Mum is cold
exam: Which sentence uses smother to mean stop someone breathing by covering their face? | «The flames were smothered by the blanket» | «Chips smothered in sauce» | «Ants smother the sugar» | *«Babies must not be smothered under heavy blankets»
